{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,23]],"date-time":"2025-10-23T20:47:03Z","timestamp":1761252423076,"version":"build-2065373602"},"reference-count":57,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"6","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2004,2,18]],"date-time":"2004-02-18T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1077062400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":5491,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Biotech &amp; Bioengineering"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1989,2,5]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title><jats:p>Dynamic reaction diffusion models were used to analyze the consequences of aggregation for syntrophic reactions in methanogenic ecosystems. Flocs from a whey digestor were used to measure all model parameters under the <jats:italic>in situ<\/jats:italic> conditions of a particular defined biological system. Fermentation simulations without adjustable parameters could precisely predict the kinetics of H<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> gas production of digestor flocs during syntrophic methanogenesis from ethanol. The results demonstrated a kinetic compartmentalization of H<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> metabolism inside the flocs. The interspecies electron transfer reaction was mildly diffusion controlled. The H<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> gas profiles across the flocs showed high H <jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> concentrations inside the flocs at any time. Simulations of the syntrophic metabolism at low substrate concentrations such as in digestors or sediments showed that it is impossible to achieve high H<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> gas turnovers at simultaneously low steady\u2010state H<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> concentrations. This showed a mechanistic contradiction in the concept of postulated low H<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> microenvironments for the anaerobic digestion process. The results of the computer experiments support the conclusion that syntrophic H<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> production may only be a side reaction of H<jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> independent interspecies electron transfer in methanogenic ecosystems.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/bit.260330612","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2005,5,27]],"date-time":"2005-05-27T13:29:48Z","timestamp":1117200588000},"page":"745-757","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":28,"title":["Control of interspecies electron transfer flow during anaerobic digestion: Dynamic diffusion reaction models for hydrogen gas transfer in microbial flocs"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"33","author":[{"given":"Sadettin S.","family":"Ozturk","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Bernhard O.","family":"Palsson","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Jurgen H.","family":"Thiele","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2004,2,18]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_1_2_2","unstructured":"F. G.PohlandandS. H.Harper inAnaerobic Digestion Proceedings of the Fourth International Symposium on Anaerobic Digestion Guangzhou China 1985."},{"key":"e_1_2_1_3_2","first-page":"84","volume":"29","author":"Sahm H.","year":"1984","journal-title":"Adv. Bioch. Eng. Biotechnol."},{"key":"e_1_2_1_4_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/bit.260220402"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_5_2","first-page":"178","volume":"37","author":"Jeris J. S.","year":"1965","journal-title":"Wat. Pol. Contr. Fed."},{"key":"e_1_2_1_6_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"180","DOI":"10.1128\/aem.51.1.180-187.1986","volume":"51","author":"Chartrain M.","year":"1986","journal-title":"Appl. Environ. Microbiol."},{"key":"e_1_2_1_7_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1098\/rstb.1982.0064"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_8_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-pag